3	// Proprietary in-portal DB manager — server actions.
4	//
5	// A Nxeon-built replacement for the Adminer file we used to drop into the
6	// customer's webroot. Everything here runs SERVER-SIDE: the customer never
7	// receives a DB credential, and every query is executed as the account's SCOPED
8	// MySQL manager user (see lib/hosting-db.ts + buildDbMgrGrantSql), which MySQL
9	// confines to this account's own `<username>_*` databases and nothing else.
10	//
11	// AUTH: every action requires the authenticated OWNER of the account (or an
12	// ADMIN). Actions that RUN SQL or reveal row data additionally call
13	// assertNotImpersonating — an admin impersonating a customer must not read or
14	// mutate that customer's live data (same discipline as revealHostingSftpPassword
15	// / createHostingDatabase). Read-only "which databases exist" listing (from OUR
16	// portal tables, not the node) is owner-or-admin without that extra bar.
